    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Au collège",
      "cefr": "A2–B1",
      "audience": "Intermédiaire · Collège",
      "description": "Articles courts, grammaire en contexte, compréhension écrite et orale.",
      "lessons": [
        {
          "id": "l2-school-day",
          "type": "article",
          "title": "Tom's school day",
          "audio": {
            "duration": 45
          },
          "text": [
            "Tom lives in Manchester. He gets up at seven o'clock every morning.",
            "He usually takes the bus to school. His favourite subject is science, but he doesn't like maths.",
            "After school, he plays football with his friends in the park."
          ],
          "grammar": {
            "title": "Present simple",
            "rule": "Habitudes : he/she/it + verbe + -s (he gets, he plays). Négation : doesn't + base verbale (he doesn't like)."
          },
          "quiz": [
            {
              "q": "Where does Tom live?",
              "choices": [
                "London",
                "Manchester",
                "Leeds"
              ],
              "answer": 1
            },
            {
              "q": "Choisis la forme correcte : « She ___ to school by bus. »",
              "choices": [
                "go",
                "goes",
                "going"
              ],
              "answer": 1
            },
            {
              "q": "Which subject does Tom dislike?",
              "choices": [
                "science",
                "maths",
                "sport"
              ],
              "answer": 1
            }
          ],
          "scene": [
            "🎒",
            "⚽",
            "🔬"
          ],
          "tint": "#99f6e4"
        },
        {
          "id": "l2-weekend",
          "type": "article",
          "title": "Last weekend",
          "audio": {
            "duration": 40
          },
          "text": [
            "Last Saturday, Emma visited her grandparents in Brighton.",
            "They walked on the beach and ate fish and chips. On Sunday, it rained, so they watched a film."
          ],
          "grammar": {
            "title": "Prétérit (past simple)",
            "rule": "Verbes réguliers : base + -ed (visited, walked). Irréguliers à apprendre : eat → ate, go → went."
          },
          "quiz": [
            {
              "q": "What did they eat?",
              "choices": [
                "pizza",
                "fish and chips",
                "sandwiches"
              ],
              "answer": 1
            },
            {
              "q": "Le prétérit de « eat » est…",
              "choices": [
                "eated",
                "ate",
                "eaten"
              ],
              "answer": 1
            }
          ],
          "scene": [
            "🏖️",
            "🐟",
            "🎬"
          ],
          "tint": "#bae6fd"
        },
        {
          "id": "l2-hobbies",
          "type": "article",
          "title": "My hobbies",
          "audio": {
            "duration": 40
          },
          "text": [
            "Hi, I'm Priya and I'm thirteen. I love reading comics and I enjoy drawing my own characters.",
            "My brother Sam is different: he hates sitting still. He loves skateboarding and he is good at swimming.",
            "At the weekend, we both like cooking pancakes with our dad."
          ],
          "grammar": {
            "title": "Love / like / enjoy / hate + -ing",
            "rule": "Après les verbes de goût, le verbe suivant prend -ing : I love reading, he hates sitting. Même chose après « good at » : good at swimming."
          },
          "quiz": [
            {
              "q": "What does Priya enjoy?",
              "choices": [
                "skateboarding",
                "drawing",
                "swimming"
              ],
              "answer": 1
            },
            {
              "q": "Complète : « Sam hates ___ still. »",
              "choices": [
                "sit",
                "to sitting",
                "sitting"
              ],
              "answer": 2
            },
            {
              "q": "What do they like doing together?",
              "choices": [
                "cooking pancakes",
                "reading comics",
                "playing football"
              ],
              "answer": 0
            }
          ],
          "scene": [
            "🎨",
            "🛹",
            "🥞"
          ],
          "tint": "#ddd6fe"
        },
        {
          "id": "l2-london",
          "type": "article",
          "title": "A trip to London",
          "audio": {
            "duration": 50
          },
          "text": [
            "Our class went to London last month. It is bigger and busier than our town!",
            "The London Eye was the most exciting part of the trip: from the top, the river Thames looked smaller than a ribbon.",
            "The museums were free, but the food was more expensive than at home."
          ],
          "grammar": {
            "title": "Comparatif et superlatif",
            "rule": "Adjectif court : big → bigger than → the biggest. Adjectif long : expensive → more expensive than → the most expensive."
          },
          "quiz": [
            {
              "q": "What was the most exciting part of the trip?",
              "choices": [
                "the museums",
                "the London Eye",
                "the food"
              ],
              "answer": 1
            },
            {
              "q": "Le comparatif de « busy » est…",
              "choices": [
                "more busy",
                "busier",
                "the busiest"
              ],
              "answer": 1
            },
            {
              "q": "The food in London was…",
              "choices": [
                "cheaper",
                "free",
                "more expensive"
              ],
              "answer": 2
            }
